WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: the task context pack was a directory
LISTING (title + `ws.list("")` head) with no budget, no provenance, no
journal awareness; crates/context was logic-only OUTSIDE the product
binary closure)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- Closure: modbit-context is now a modbit-core-runtime dependency
  (17 of 26 modbit-* crates in the product closure).
- build_context_pack rewritten through the canonical context engine:
  * fragments packed value-ordered under a token-derived character
    budget (max_input_tokens * 4 chars, clamped 2k..64k) by
    modbit-context pack_with_budget — critical task brief reserved
    FIRST and retained even under pressure; overflow compresses into
    digest-addressed hydratable handles;
  * EVERY packed fragment carries provenance (source, sha256 of the
    packed text, workspace revision, retrieval reason) and the envelope
    is VALIDATED by modbit-context's provenance module before shipping;
    a validation failure falls back to the brief alone, loudly (never
    ships an unattributable pack silently);
  * NEW "recently changed files" section: latest state per path from
    the workspace change journal (kind, workspace revision, content
    digest), newest first, bounded 10;
  * index-seeded file heads: the task objective queries the live
    repository index (top 8 fused hits); each contributes a bounded
    head read FRESH through the workspace service (hydration discipline
    — the index never supplies bytes).
- MOD-CTX-001 retrieve-before-edit gate: change.propose is REFUSED with
  a typed result (gate=retrieve_before_edit) naming the path and the
  remedy unless the path carries retrieval evidence in the task. The
  evidence set is recorded by fs.read, context.query hits,
  search.grep matches, search.symbol defs/refs, and context-pack
  membership (a packed file IS retrieved context). When no index tracks
  evidence the gate stays OPEN and the result says so (tracking
  unavailable — never a silent bypass). change.apply keeps its own
  unique-match + revision guards (the phase item gates propose, the
  preview step; apply remains the enforcement point for writes).

